t 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids in Martin County has a record back to 1951, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 40 of 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle ran 58% of normal in August to September and 56% in September to October. So far in 2026 it sits at 55% in March to April and 114% in June to July. Grid 19113 has a preliminary estimate of 50.3 for August to September 2026, which RMA&rsquo;s final index can change.</p>"}
